        "heading": "Eight good team names",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator, from eight different styles:</p><ul><li><strong>Sock Drawer Rovers</strong>: a proper football club ending with a joke in front, for a five-a-side team that doesn't take itself too seriously.</li><li><strong>Midnight Raptors</strong>: a time and an animal, the classic pattern for a team that wants to sound fierce.</li><li><strong>Quarterly Heroes</strong>: office language turned into a team name everyone at work will get.</li><li><strong>Mighty Minnows</strong>: small fish, big spirit, and easy for young children to cheer.</li><li><strong>Ring Leaders</strong>: a netball pun on the goal ring, and a promise to lead the league.</li><li><strong>Rain Stopped Play</strong>: the phrase every British cricketer knows too well.</li><li><strong>Wrong Captain Again</strong>: a fantasy football name that every mini-league will recognise.</li><li><strong>The Red Lion Darts Team</strong>: the pub and the game, the way pub league teams have always been named.</li></ul>"
